{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03046",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.93,
      "end_seconds": 6.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.39,
      "end_seconds": 12.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.35,
      "end_seconds": 20.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.6,
      "end_seconds": 25.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.56,
      "end_seconds": 41.75,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "I, I wanted to get a tight chest at work looked at. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.89,
      "end_seconds": 45.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.84,
      "end_seconds": 56.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "It's been two weeks now. Oh, and a cough that eases on holiday. That's been about the same, six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.67,
      "end_seconds": 79.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Any weight loss, fever, coughing up blood or ankle swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.74,
      "end_seconds": 87.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "ah, no, no weight loss, fever, coughing up blood or ankle swelling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.0,
      "end_seconds": 92.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "right, on the the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.85,
      "end_seconds": 94.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.74,
      "end_seconds": 98.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.6,
      "end_seconds": 105.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "No, you know, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.21,
      "end_seconds": 109.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.71,
      "end_seconds": 119.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.21,
      "end_seconds": 123.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.61,
      "end_seconds": 129.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.63,
      "end_seconds": 132.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.27,
      "end_seconds": 137.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.55,
      "end_seconds": 142.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.32,
      "end_seconds": 146.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.98,
      "end_seconds": 149.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "And for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.57,
      "end_seconds": 168.05,
      "duration_seconds": 15.48,
      "text": "For about a year. Carvedilol. I take it it 6.25 milligrams, twice a day for my heart. I told my wife I'd come today. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.58,
      "end_seconds": 169.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.6,
      "end_seconds": 174.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "I'm on atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.92,
      "end_seconds": 192.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.1,
      "end_seconds": 207.82,
      "duration_seconds": 14.72,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid, for about ten years. I've been putting this off for weeks. I just want to get back to normal, really. I've got heart failure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.5,
      "end_seconds": 210.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.83,
      "end_seconds": 226.03,
      "duration_seconds": 14.2,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol, for about ten years. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.25,
      "end_seconds": 237.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Alright, heart failure, that matches what I have here. Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.23,
      "end_seconds": 242.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.12,
      "end_seconds": 246.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.8,
      "end_seconds": 251.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.79,
      "end_seconds": 271.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.44,
      "end_seconds": 282.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.14,
      "end_seconds": 314.04,
      "duration_seconds": 9.9,
      "text": "Okay: temp 37.0 degrees, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, respiratory rate 15. And And pulse 70, pressure 112 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.68,
      "end_seconds": 317.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Is that that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.19,
      "end_seconds": 323.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.59,
      "end_seconds": 329.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.7,
      "end_seconds": 336.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.26,
      "end_seconds": 341.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.15,
      "end_seconds": 361.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "There is a little wheeze at the end of each breath out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.89,
      "end_seconds": 379.2,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Having listened and examined, I'd lean towards occupational asthma. It could also be COPD, so we'll keep that open. I'm sending you for spirometry because of wheeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.73,
      "end_seconds": 383.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Mm, you know, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.84,
      "end_seconds": 397.61,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "I'm going to order serial peak flow readings, for work-related wheeze. You'll be taking beclometasone inhaler, 200 micrograms, twice a day, long term. That should help with asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.51,
      "end_seconds": 399.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "mm, alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.02,
      "end_seconds": 418.16,
      "duration_seconds": 17.14,
      "text": "record peak flows at work and and at home for four weeks. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. We'll catch up in four weeks. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.36,
      "end_seconds": 422.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "no, that's all thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.78,
      "end_seconds": 428.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}